(1547170, 205065, 38925, '<td valign="top">i like it, amazing colours, good luck</td>', 'i like it, amazing colours, good luck', '2005-07-19 18:10:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547171, 204761, 35357, '<td valign="top">OH MY!  What''s up with that?  That''s just painful to look at, I hope it''s OK.  That ''kink'' in the neck cooperates nicely with the composition of your photo, or vice-versa.  Nice dof too.  But man, OUCH!  Good catch.</td>', 'OH MY!  What''s up with that?  That''s just painful to look at, I hope it''s OK.  That ''kink'' in the neck cooperates nicely with the composition of your photo, or vice-versa.  Nice dof too.  But man, OUCH!  Good catch.', '2005-07-19 18:11:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547179, 204555, 35357, '<td valign="top">I like the repetition and dof!  Really nice catch, definitely a keeper. You''re forcing me to give you a 10.</td>', 'I like the repetition and dof!  Really nice catch, definitely a keeper. You''re forcing me to give you a 10.', '2005-07-19 18:14:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547188, 204790, 35357, '<td valign="top">Great use of colour tone and natural frame, very nice.  I''ll bet the lighting was tough too, not that you''d know from the photo, though.  Geat job.  If I stare long enough I can see him scratching his bum on the wall.</td>', 'Great use of colour tone and natural frame, very nice.  I''ll bet the lighting was tough too, not that you''d know from the photo, though.  Geat job.  If I stare long enough I can see him scratching his bum on the wall.', '2005-07-19 18:17:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547206, 204467, 35357, '<td valign="top">I like the subject and the setting.  I''m afraid the lighting was poor, as I can''t see the bug very well.  For a shot like this I''d prefer to see it much closer to the subject, at least from bum to the tip of the antenna, it''s easy to see it''s on popcorn at a crop like that.  Good try &amp; good luck!  Oh yeah, I would throw that popcorn out if I wear you ;-)</td>', 'I like the subject and the setting.  I''m afraid the lighting was poor, as I can''t see the bug very well.  For a shot like this I''d prefer to see it much closer to the subject, at least from bum to the tip of the antenna, it''s easy to see it''s on popcorn at a crop like that.  Good try & good luck!  Oh yeah, I would throw that popcorn out if I wear you ;-)', '2005-07-19 18:23:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547217, 204567, 35357, '<td valign="top">I love the lighting you''ve captured, wonderful shot.  I think you chose the perfect focus for it.  Very warm, calm, &amp; soft feeling.  Two udders up from me.</td>', 'I love the lighting you''ve captured, wonderful shot.  I think you chose the perfect focus for it.  Very warm, calm, & soft feeling.  Two udders up from me.', '2005-07-19 18:26:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547237, 205079, 35357, '<td valign="top">This photo looks pretty funky to me.  Looks like the fox(?) was Photoshopped onto a gradational background.  Something about it just doesn''t look natural to me.  Also looks like the fox is dead &amp; stuffed.  Anyway, moving on from my confusion... I think your composition would be improved with a crop on the left, just a little away from its ear.  That would bring the viewer''s eye more easily from its glass eye &amp; down along the body.  OK, I have to move on now, your photo is starting to freak me out! :-D</td>', 'This photo looks pretty funky to me.  Looks like the fox(?) was Photoshopped onto a gradational background.  Something about it just doesn''t look natural to me.  Also looks like the fox is dead & stuffed.  Anyway, moving on from my confusion... I think your composition would be improved with a crop on the left, just a little away from its ear.  That would bring the viewer''s eye more easily from its glass eye & down along the body.  OK, I have to move on now, your photo is starting to freak me out! :-D', '2005-07-19 18:35:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547253, 205289, 35357, '<td valign="top">For the next challenge use the full 640 pixels allowed.  Don''t make me come over there!  Don''t make me get up &amp; come over there!  But seriuosly folks.... I like the composition, though it''s a bit small for me to see much else as per focus etc.  The subject is very nice, of course, I love cheetahs.  I would prefer a shallower depth of field to blur out the background, but I can''t even do that with the camera I have, so don''t expect it of anyone, just something else for me to type just in case you have a camera capable of it, and another way for me to complain about my camera.</td>', 'For the next challenge use the full 640 pixels allowed.  Don''t make me come over there!  Don''t make me get up & come over there!  But seriuosly folks.... I like the composition, though it''s a bit small for me to see much else as per focus etc.  The subject is very nice, of course, I love cheetahs.  I would prefer a shallower depth of field to blur out the background, but I can''t even do that with the camera I have, so don''t expect it of anyone, just something else for me to type just in case you have a camera capable of it, and another way for me to complain about my camera.', '2005-07-19 18:42:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547284, 205429, 35357, '<td valign="top">Selective desat wants to make the animal the subject, but its facing the wrong way.  Girls is fighting to be the main subject, but is B&amp;W.  I''d prefer the crop to the girl''s elbow, would help the composition a bit, I think.  Focus is very crisp, even far into the background from what I can tell, pulls a bit of attention away from the foreground.  Mostly, I suggest you use the full 640 pixel width allowed, it makes a world of difference to the viewer.  I like how the beast (donkey?) is coming into the photo, good eye on that.  I think there''s a lot of potential here if there were no desat, or totally B&amp;W &amp; the girls were moved to get a better view of the donkey nose &amp; the girls arm &amp; hand feeding it.  Just so you know I''m not hammering your photo, it is nice, I''m giving it a 6.</td>', 'Selective desat wants to make the animal the subject, but its facing the wrong way.  Girls is fighting to be the main subject, but is B&W.  I''d prefer the crop to the girl''s elbow, would help the composition a bit, I think.  Focus is very crisp, even far into the background from what I can tell, pulls a bit of attention away from the foreground.  Mostly, I suggest you use the full 640 pixel width allowed, it makes a world of difference to the viewer.  I like how the beast (donkey?) is coming into the photo, good eye on that.  I think there''s a lot of potential here if there were no desat, or totally B&W & the girls were moved to get a better view of the donkey nose & the girls arm & hand feeding it.  Just so you know I''m not hammering your photo, it is nice, I''m giving it a 6.', '2005-07-19 18:54:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547322, 205219, 36309, '<td valign="top">Nice capture - to me he looks like an old man with cape and staff</td>', 'Nice capture - to me he looks like an old man with cape and staff', '2005-07-19 19:09:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547326, 204701, 36309, '<td valign="top">Massive attitude - well captured!</td>', 'Massive attitude - well captured!', '2005-07-19 19:10:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547327, 205287, 35357, '<td valign="top">Fantastic shot for several reasons.  I think tigers are absolutely the coolest and you''ve really got a great focus on the colours.  It''s pose is very tense, and you''ve added to it marvelously with the framing space to the right.  The black background looks a little funky where it meets the grass, to the point of appearing Photoshopped, but the black sure does set off the orange &amp; black of the tiger.</td>', 'Fantastic shot for several reasons.  I think tigers are absolutely the coolest and you''ve really got a great focus on the colours.  It''s pose is very tense, and you''ve added to it marvelously with the framing space to the right.  The black background looks a little funky where it meets the grass, to the point of appearing Photoshopped, but the black sure does set off the orange & black of the tiger.', '2005-07-19 19:10:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547331, 205086, 36309, '<td valign="top">Very humorous!</td>', 'Very humorous!', '2005-07-19 19:11:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547334, 205287, 37409, '<td valign="top">Great color on the tiget but bad job with the PS work on the background.</td>', 'Great color on the tiget but bad job with the PS work on the background.', '2005-07-19 19:12:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547335, 203855, 35357, '<td valign="top">640 pixels is allowed for image size &amp; you''ll find that you fare much better when you use full size.  The photo is quite dark. [6]</td>', '640 pixels is allowed for image size & you''ll find that you fare much better when you use full size.  The photo is quite dark. [6]', '2005-07-19 19:13:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547342, 203815, 35357, '<td valign="top">Great texture shot. I like the composition too.</td>', 'Great texture shot. I like the composition too.', '2005-07-19 19:14:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547344, 205429, 36309, '<td valign="top">Would this have been improved if at least one of their faces was visible so that the viewer could see their expression?</td>', 'Would this have been improved if at least one of their faces was visible so that the viewer could see their expression?', '2005-07-19 19:15:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547345, 205342, 35357, '<td valign="top">Fantastic quality.  Great job.  Sorry, but that''s all I have to say.  Good luck! [10]</td>', 'Fantastic quality.  Great job.  Sorry, but that''s all I have to say.  Good luck! [10]', '2005-07-19 19:15:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547349, 205244, 36309, '<td valign="top">Title fits the expression very well!</td>', 'Title fits the expression very well!', '2005-07-19 19:16:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547351, 204494, 39676, '<td valign="top">That''s is scary.</td>', 'That''s is scary.', '2005-07-19 19:17:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547353, 203613, 12240, '<td valign="top">simply,lovely,his face shows a human expression.I really liked it, Congrats!</td>', 'simply,lovely,his face shows a human expression.I really liked it, Congrats!', '2005-07-19 19:18:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547360, 204748, 12240, '<td valign="top">a beautiful picture with a perfect sense i its title.I loved this one. Congrats!!</td>', 'a beautiful picture with a perfect sense i its title.I loved this one. Congrats!!', '2005-07-19 19:21:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547363, 205077, 12240, '<td valign="top">Its my missing aunt!! tell me where is she? Beautiful!</td>', 'Its my missing aunt!! tell me where is she? Beautiful!', '2005-07-19 19:23:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547367, 204029, 35161, '<td valign="top">A wonderful sharp image of this little owl with a beautiful plumage! <br/>Very nice! :)</td>', 'A wonderful sharp image of this little owl with a beautiful plumage! Very nice! :)', '2005-07-19 19:24:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547369, 204920, 35161, '<td valign="top">A wonderful portrait of this beautiful creature....<br/>....but a sad title... :(<br/>Very, very well captured! :)</td>', 'A wonderful portrait of this beautiful creature........but a sad title... :(Very, very well captured! :)', '2005-07-19 19:26:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547370, 205014, 35357, '<td valign="top">That''s a great pose of a great beast.  Wonderful composition too.  Probably without all the Photoshopping I''d give this a 10.  Unfortunately, you''re at the mercy of the phillistine masses, of which I am one.  The way this poor lionized lion looks, I''d expect to see it on a fuzzy blanket at a flea market.  I''m going to find out where you live after the challenge ends, and come &amp; take your silly lionizing filter away from you.  Though you don''t deserve it after slaughtering this photo, i''m going to give you a 7 anyway, just because I like you.  Don''t let me catch you lionizing any more lions or I''ll report you to the SPCA.  That also goes for womanizing any women!</td>', 'That''s a great pose of a great beast.  Wonderful composition too.  Probably without all the Photoshopping I''d give this a 10.  Unfortunately, you''re at the mercy of the phillistine masses, of which I am one.  The way this poor lionized lion looks, I''d expect to see it on a fuzzy blanket at a flea market.  I''m going to find out where you live after the challenge ends, and come & take your silly lionizing filter away from you.  Though you don''t deserve it after slaughtering this photo, i''m going to give you a 7 anyway, just because I like you.  Don''t let me catch you lionizing any more lions or I''ll report you to the SPCA.  That also goes for womanizing any women!', '2005-07-19 19:27:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547463, 204494, 37320, '<td valign="top">jEEPERS!  Good shot!</td>', 'jEEPERS!  Good shot!', '2005-07-19 20:04:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547493, 203143, 34659, '<td valign="top">Nice expression and interesting composition, but the whites are all blown out.  Might try turning down the backlighting and adjusting contrast, etc. to reduce the glare.  Otherwise nice shot.</td>', 'Nice expression and interesting composition, but the whites are all blown out.  Might try turning down the backlighting and adjusting contrast, etc. to reduce the glare.  Otherwise nice shot.', '2005-07-19 20:14:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547501, 205314, 34659, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot.  Really like the wings &amp; motion.  Nice color tones too.  The eye looks like it''s been PSed pretty hardily though.  Perhaps it''s me and the eye is naturally that red, but I don''t remember spoonbills having eyes quite that vivid.  Still, a nice shot.</td>', 'Beautiful shot.  Really like the wings & motion.  Nice color tones too.  The eye looks like it''s been PSed pretty hardily though.  Perhaps it''s me and the eye is naturally that red, but I don''t remember spoonbills having eyes quite that vivid.  Still, a nice shot.', '2005-07-19 20:16:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547507, 205077, 34659, '<td valign="top">I almost entered a shot of this guy''s cousins (African Black Crowned Cranes).  You''ve got good DOF in the shot, but you lose a lot of detail in the blown out highlights.  Also, I think you could crop it closer to bring out more definition in the bird and bump up the washed out colors.  Don''t get me wrong, it''s still a pretty good shot...</td>', 'I almost entered a shot of this guy''s cousins (African Black Crowned Cranes).  You''ve got good DOF in the shot, but you lose a lot of detail in the blown out highlights.  Also, I think you could crop it closer to bring out more definition in the bird and bump up the washed out colors.  Don''t get me wrong, it''s still a pretty good shot...', '2005-07-19 20:18:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547510, 205317, 34659, '<td valign="top">What a cutie!  Wish the lighting didn''t wash out the color quite as much, but you''ve got good DOF and nice composition.</td>', 'What a cutie!  Wish the lighting didn''t wash out the color quite as much, but you''ve got good DOF and nice composition.', '2005-07-19 20:20:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547515, 205219, 34659, '<td valign="top">This shot has a LOT of character.  Nice capture.  The blown highlights and harsh lighting are a distraction though.  You lose a lot of definition and color due to that.  Otherwise, I think it''s great.</td>', 'This shot has a LOT of character.  Nice capture.  The blown highlights and harsh lighting are a distraction though.  You lose a lot of definition and color due to that.  Otherwise, I think it''s great.', '2005-07-19 20:21:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547518, 202828, 34659, '<td valign="top">Good DOF  and color.  You pushed the envelope with the lighting/highlights so that they''re just on the edge of being blown out, but I think you pulled it off.  Nice detail and composition too.</td>', 'Good DOF  and color.  You pushed the envelope with the lighting/highlights so that they''re just on the edge of being blown out, but I think you pulled it off.  Nice detail and composition too.', '2005-07-19 20:22:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547527, 205267, 34659, '<td valign="top">Orangutans are such fun creatures!  (Almost too human too - I hate to see them caged, but that''s another story!)  :-)<br/> <br/>Nice shot - maybe a little oversharpened and I''d like to see a little more of the guy (crop is a little tight), but good expression.  Not crazy about the border either, but it''s hard to go wrong when shooting these guys.</td>', 'Orangutans are such fun creatures!  (Almost too human too - I hate to see them caged, but that''s another story!)  :-) Nice shot - maybe a little oversharpened and I''d like to see a little more of the guy (crop is a little tight), but good expression.  Not crazy about the border either, but it''s hard to go wrong when shooting these guys.', '2005-07-19 20:25:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547532, 204773, 34659, '<td valign="top">Nice unique entry.  I wish the highlights weren''t blown out and the blue overtones were turned down a notch though.  Good composition and I think the border is fine.</td>', 'Nice unique entry.  I wish the highlights weren''t blown out and the blue overtones were turned down a notch though.  Good composition and I think the border is fine.', '2005-07-19 20:26:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547540, 204502, 34659, '<td valign="top">I love Muscovy ducks!  I grew up around a lot of them (they''re quite prolific!).  Excellent use of selective color and your detail is exquisite.  I''m not crazy about the crop or the border, but this is an exceptionally good shot.  Nice work.  Bumping up.</td>', 'I love Muscovy ducks!  I grew up around a lot of them (they''re quite prolific!).  Excellent use of selective color and your detail is exquisite.  I''m not crazy about the crop or the border, but this is an exceptionally good shot.  Nice work.  Bumping up.', '2005-07-19 20:29:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547546, 204555, 34659, '<td valign="top">Cute shot &amp; caption.  Great DOF and color, although I think the crop is a little too tight.</td>', 'Cute shot & caption.  Great DOF and color, although I think the crop is a little too tight.', '2005-07-19 20:30:25.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(1547595, 205148, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2<br/>Color/Contrast: 2/2<br/>Composition: 2/2<br/>Photo Quality: 2/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 1/2<br/> <br/>Very nice photo here. Colors are well exposed, picture is very clear and sharp. I am just not a big fan of the composition.</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2Color/Contrast: 2/2Composition: 2/2Photo Quality: 2/2My Subjective Affinity: 1/2 Very nice photo here. Colors are well exposed, picture is very clear and sharp. I am just not a big fan of the composition.', '2005-07-19 20:48:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547599, 205215, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2<br/>Color/Contrast: 2/2<br/>Composition: 2/2<br/>Photo Quality: 2/2<br/>My Subjecitve Affinity: 2/2<br/> <br/>Excellent work. I would not say that this is the most stunning photo of all, but it is really nice, and I still give it a 10 in the various areas. Nice work.</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2Color/Contrast: 2/2Composition: 2/2Photo Quality: 2/2My Subjecitve Affinity: 2/2 Excellent work. I would not say that this is the most stunning photo of all, but it is really nice, and I still give it a 10 in the various areas. Nice work.', '2005-07-19 20:50:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547604, 205267, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2<br/>Color/Contrast: 2/2<br/>Composition: 2/2<br/>Photo Quality: 1/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 2/2<br/> <br/>Really nice photo. Even with a not so glamorous background, this is an excellent shot. The look on his face is awesome! Nice work.</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2Color/Contrast: 2/2Composition: 2/2Photo Quality: 1/2My Subjective Affinity: 2/2 Really nice photo. Even with a not so glamorous background, this is an excellent shot. The look on his face is awesome! Nice work.', '2005-07-19 20:52:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547607, 205379, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2<br/>Color/Contrast: 2/2<br/>Composition: 2/2<br/>Photo Quality: 2/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 2/2<br/> <br/>Nice work on this one. Everything is very well exposed, even with what appears to be a very bright, sunny day. Good job!</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2Color/Contrast: 2/2Composition: 2/2Photo Quality: 2/2My Subjective Affinity: 2/2 Nice work on this one. Everything is very well exposed, even with what appears to be a very bright, sunny day. Good job!', '2005-07-19 20:54:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547609, 205423, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2<br/>Color/Contrast: 1/2<br/>Composition: 1/2<br/>Photo Quality: 2/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 1/2</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2Color/Contrast: 1/2Composition: 1/2Photo Quality: 2/2My Subjective Affinity: 1/2', '2005-07-19 20:55:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547682, 204632, 35357, '<td valign="top">Neat shot, I like the vibrant colours and reach of the bird across the frame.  I also like the frame, it sets off the photo nicely.</td>', 'Neat shot, I like the vibrant colours and reach of the bird across the frame.  I also like the frame, it sets off the photo nicely.', '2005-07-19 21:17:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547696, 205362, 35357, '<td valign="top">I''ll bet you get a fair number of comments on this one.  This is the kind of shot I might submit for kicks, so bravo to you for that.  It''s nice to see something different so I can take a break and write my sorry excuse of a comment.  I admire the way you trained two flies to look one way, and two to look the other way, that must have taken a lot of time &amp; patience.  I''m assuming this shot was taken in England, as the flies are keeping left rather than right, except for that one fly which is obviously on his way home from the pub.</td>', 'I''ll bet you get a fair number of comments on this one.  This is the kind of shot I might submit for kicks, so bravo to you for that.  It''s nice to see something different so I can take a break and write my sorry excuse of a comment.  I admire the way you trained two flies to look one way, and two to look the other way, that must have taken a lot of time & patience.  I''m assuming this shot was taken in England, as the flies are keeping left rather than right, except for that one fly which is obviously on his way home from the pub.', '2005-07-19 21:23:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547711, 205172, 35357, '<td valign="top">This is a nice, crisp shot complete with decent depth of field.  Pretty nice composition too, though I would have cropped just to the right of its head.  This photo would do much, much better if you had used the full 640 pixel size allowed.  Definitely a nice shot, but very few will give you a decent score due to size alone.  I suggest you read up on sizing your photos for the competitions in the tutorials section, I think you''ll do much better on the next challenge you submit to if you use the full 640 pixels.  I''m giving you a 6, but you likely would have got an 8 or 9 if this were bigger.</td>', 'This is a nice, crisp shot complete with decent depth of field.  Pretty nice composition too, though I would have cropped just to the right of its head.  This photo would do much, much better if you had used the full 640 pixel size allowed.  Definitely a nice shot, but very few will give you a decent score due to size alone.  I suggest you read up on sizing your photos for the competitions in the tutorials section, I think you''ll do much better on the next challenge you submit to if you use the full 640 pixels.  I''m giving you a 6, but you likely would have got an 8 or 9 if this were bigger.', '2005-07-19 21:29:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547715, 204911, 35357, '<td valign="top">The lighting/darkness makes it tough to see any detail.</td>', 'The lighting/darkness makes it tough to see any detail.', '2005-07-19 21:30:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547721, 205359, 35357, '<td valign="top">I can almost hear the howl.  What a great shot.  Great choice of framing.</td>', 'I can almost hear the howl.  What a great shot.  Great choice of framing.', '2005-07-19 21:34:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1547724, 205219, 35357, '<td valign="top">Looks like a Wise Man with cloak and staff.  I like the studious expression.  Nice catch.</td>', 'Looks like a Wise Man with cloak and staff.  I like the studious expression.  Nice catch.', '2005-07-19 21:36:41.000000', NULL, 1),
