(1549317, 203787, 13602, '<td valign="top">Umm looks like I am not alone thinking cows should have a place in a zoo :)) I bet you also get all the comments that this is not a zoo animal, Good luck!</td>', 'Umm looks like I am not alone thinking cows should have a place in a zoo :)) I bet you also get all the comments that this is not a zoo animal, Good luck!', '2005-07-20 07:31:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1549393, 204632, 16053, '<td valign="top">The eye is very sharp but it seems a litle soft in the contour of the head. Good color and position. Love the detail in the eye and in the nose</td>', 'The eye is very sharp but it seems a litle soft in the contour of the head. Good color and position. Love the detail in the eye and in the nose', '2005-07-20 08:07:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1549396, 204933, 16053, '<td valign="top">Terrific photo. exelent control of light. A top ten certainly.</td>', 'Terrific photo. exelent control of light. A top ten certainly.', '2005-07-20 08:08:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1549463, 205269, 23614, '<td valign="top">Very good composition. Nice contrast. A bit too much noise and would have been nice to see the eyes a bit more in focus. Well done!</td>', 'Very good composition. Nice contrast. A bit too much noise and would have been nice to see the eyes a bit more in focus. Well done!', '2005-07-20 08:48:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1549531, 205350, 16053, '<td valign="top">excellent subject and high key tipe of shoot. Love the photo.</td>', 'excellent subject and high key tipe of shoot. Love the photo.', '2005-07-20 09:41:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1549669, 204176, 36068, '<td valign="top">I love the title</td>', 'I love the title', '2005-07-20 10:33:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1549677, 203765, 36068, '<td valign="top">I love the Blue Footed Booby....great picture!!</td>', 'I love the Blue Footed Booby....great picture!!', '2005-07-20 10:35:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1549685, 205460, 36068, '<td valign="top">Oh goodness...this is funny</td>', 'Oh goodness...this is funny', '2005-07-20 10:37:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1549692, 202814, 36068, '<td valign="top">Beautiful picture!</td>', 'Beautiful picture!', '2005-07-20 10:38:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1549845, 205253, 33560, '<td valign="top">Perfect composition, framing - perfectly cropped.  Nice color pallete.   Excellent</td>', 'Perfect composition, framing - perfectly cropped.  Nice color pallete.   Excellent', '2005-07-20 11:24:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1549859, 204634, 33560, '<td valign="top">Focus could be a little sharper, especially on those attractive whiskers. (some sharpening would help.)  I''m finding the left side of the photo and the bottom (both senses) not to add much, so I wonder whether it might be improved by cropping.  I love the three color sensibitlity of the photo.</td>', 'Focus could be a little sharper, especially on those attractive whiskers. (some sharpening would help.)  I''m finding the left side of the photo and the bottom (both senses) not to add much, so I wonder whether it might be improved by cropping.  I love the three color sensibitlity of the photo.', '2005-07-20 11:27:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1549868, 204320, 33560, '<td valign="top">Great Bokeh.  I really like the way the wire is used to add structure to the photo.  Nice choice to use B&amp;W.</td>', 'Great Bokeh.  I really like the way the wire is used to add structure to the photo.  Nice choice to use B&W.', '2005-07-20 11:29:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1549897, 205458, 33560, '<td valign="top">It captures the texture of the elephant very nidely.  And his expression.  I''m a little unsure the slurping water adds anything.    Not that the photographer had any choice in this, but there is somethng about the  nature of the background that seems wrong - I think it has to do with the green overpowering the subject.  And I wonder whether this would be better in B&amp;W.</td>', 'It captures the texture of the elephant very nidely.  And his expression.  I''m a little unsure the slurping water adds anything.    Not that the photographer had any choice in this, but there is somethng about the  nature of the background that seems wrong - I think it has to do with the green overpowering the subject.  And I wonder whether this would be better in B&W.', '2005-07-20 11:32:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1549927, 205423, 33560, '<td valign="top">The shallow DOF is perfect, Focus sharp.   Good choice to give the cheetah room to roam on the left side, but I wonder whether the photo might be just the tiniest bit less static if some were shaved off the right side.</td>', 'The shallow DOF is perfect, Focus sharp.   Good choice to give the cheetah room to roam on the left side, but I wonder whether the photo might be just the tiniest bit less static if some were shaved off the right side.', '2005-07-20 11:36:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1549960, 204701, 33560, '<td valign="top">You say tomayto; I say tomahto.   The expression is priceless. I love the shape and the way it is framed: it is cropped very carefully.   The rich tonal variation on his neck and chest is exquisite.  I''m a little wierd about finding colors distracting  - but I wonder if you considered desaturating greens and reds so there is less distraction in the BG.  In any case, it''s a super photo.  I''m green with envy.</td>', 'You say tomayto; I say tomahto.   The expression is priceless. I love the shape and the way it is framed: it is cropped very carefully.   The rich tonal variation on his neck and chest is exquisite.  I''m a little wierd about finding colors distracting  - but I wonder if you considered desaturating greens and reds so there is less distraction in the BG.  In any case, it''s a super photo.  I''m green with envy.', '2005-07-20 11:42:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1550003, 204146, 33560, '<td valign="top">I find that when I go into the yard to take photos of things I inevitably find weeds in the way and few photos get started without some preliminary weeding.  In this case, I think a pruning sheers would have helped much, for the subject is upstaged by ten brightly lit leaves.  And speaking of pruning,  I''m not finding anything in the left third of the photo that adds anything.    The subject has a cute face and is placed very artfully in the tree.  Unfortunately the harsh lighting keeps us from seing any textures in his coat - especially in the shadows. So the subject ceases to be a stuffed animal, but becomes a caricature of a stuffed animal.    This might have worked tho your advantage if somehow the rest of the photo had been made a caricature as well ( not sure what this would mean in practice.)</td>', 'I find that when I go into the yard to take photos of things I inevitably find weeds in the way and few photos get started without some preliminary weeding.  In this case, I think a pruning sheers would have helped much, for the subject is upstaged by ten brightly lit leaves.  And speaking of pruning,  I''m not finding anything in the left third of the photo that adds anything.    The subject has a cute face and is placed very artfully in the tree.  Unfortunately the harsh lighting keeps us from seing any textures in his coat - especially in the shadows. So the subject ceases to be a stuffed animal, but becomes a caricature of a stuffed animal.    This might have worked tho your advantage if somehow the rest of the photo had been made a caricature as well ( not sure what this would mean in practice.)', '2005-07-20 11:53:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1550022, 204827, 33560, '<td valign="top">Vewwwy big puddy tat!  Every bit of the execution of this photo is perfectly done.  The framing is perfect. The focus is perfect.  The background is very strongly blurred.  The subject is compelling.  It''s a really good photo, yet there is something about it which bothers me.  It has something to do with that big white blotch in the background.  I think if that big white blotch were all through te background the photo would be better.  And I think if it were not there at all the photo would be better.  And I completely reallize that in photos such as this, one simply has no control over these sorts of things.</td>', 'Vewwwy big puddy tat!  Every bit of the execution of this photo is perfectly done.  The framing is perfect. The focus is perfect.  The background is very strongly blurred.  The subject is compelling.  It''s a really good photo, yet there is something about it which bothers me.  It has something to do with that big white blotch in the background.  I think if that big white blotch were all through te background the photo would be better.  And I think if it were not there at all the photo would be better.  And I completely reallize that in photos such as this, one simply has no control over these sorts of things.', '2005-07-20 12:00:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1550049, 205446, 33560, '<td valign="top">Wow, great use of lighting.  It''s a very attractive subject.  The bokeh is very nice.  Crisp focus everywhere except for a few strands in the upper left.  Given DPC''s usual tendency to slam lack of sharpness, I''d have been tempted to crop the photo so it is vertical, but I suppose this might do too much violence to that glorious luminescent crown.</td>', 'Wow, great use of lighting.  It''s a very attractive subject.  The bokeh is very nice.  Crisp focus everywhere except for a few strands in the upper left.  Given DPC''s usual tendency to slam lack of sharpness, I''d have been tempted to crop the photo so it is vertical, but I suppose this might do too much violence to that glorious luminescent crown.', '2005-07-20 12:08:20.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(1550052, 205250, 33560, '<td valign="top">The subject seems a little dark. Everything else seems a little confusing.</td>', 'The subject seems a little dark. Everything else seems a little confusing.', '2005-07-20 12:09:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1550062, 203438, 22689, '<td valign="top">Cute but with a too small size .</td>', 'Cute but with a too small size .', '2005-07-20 12:12:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1550071, 205343, 33560, '<td valign="top">The subject is interesting and attractive. The lighting does a great  job describing to the viewer the shape of the crane.  Unfortunately, most of us are used to wildlife shots of birds that more completely blur the background.   Fortunately this background is full of fine-textured things, but somehow enough of that texture is evident to  distract one''s attentions from the subject. Finally I find the cranberry splotch on the crane clashes a tiny bit with the yellowish green of the background and find myself wondering whether a touch of selective desaturation would not fix this problem.</td>', 'The subject is interesting and attractive. The lighting does a great  job describing to the viewer the shape of the crane.  Unfortunately, most of us are used to wildlife shots of birds that more completely blur the background.   Fortunately this background is full of fine-textured things, but somehow enough of that texture is evident to  distract one''s attentions from the subject. Finally I find the cranberry splotch on the crane clashes a tiny bit with the yellowish green of the background and find myself wondering whether a touch of selective desaturation would not fix this problem.', '2005-07-20 12:17:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1550074, 204743, 33560, '<td valign="top">The beak is very nicely focussed, but both eyes appear to be fuzzy.  Nice ''expression.''</td>', 'The beak is very nicely focussed, but both eyes appear to be fuzzy.  Nice ''expression.''', '2005-07-20 12:19:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1550083, 205082, 33560, '<td valign="top">I love the way the wire fence frames the eyes.  We are left with a strong impression that the bird is a sentient being and that she  sits flightless but safe behind this fence sadly dreaming of a wide open range.  For the first minute I spent with this photo I strongly resented that the wire cut off her beak.  And then I discovered that this sentiment somehow put me metaphorically on the same side of the fence as the captive.  Now all I can say is Bravo.  It''s brilliant.</td>', 'I love the way the wire fence frames the eyes.  We are left with a strong impression that the bird is a sentient being and that she  sits flightless but safe behind this fence sadly dreaming of a wide open range.  For the first minute I spent with this photo I strongly resented that the wire cut off her beak.  And then I discovered that this sentiment somehow put me metaphorically on the same side of the fence as the captive.  Now all I can say is Bravo.  It''s brilliant.', '2005-07-20 12:25:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1550104, 205219, 33560, '<td valign="top">Great expression.  Super lighting. Great composition. <br/> <br/>We wonder what became of the background behind the subject (is it some kind of large, reflective surface?), but cannot regret that it is gone.  We only wonder why the same force was not at work on the other side of the telephone pole.</td>', 'Great expression.  Super lighting. Great composition.  We wonder what became of the background behind the subject (is it some kind of large, reflective surface?), but cannot regret that it is gone.  We only wonder why the same force was not at work on the other side of the telephone pole.', '2005-07-20 12:32:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1550126, 204585, 33560, '<td valign="top">Color, line, lighting, and composition are super.  While I greatly appreciate the extreme softness of the background, I do wish the neck of the bird were not quite so out of focus.  While the bird''s eye is the natural focal point of the piece, man''s eye is naturally drawn to the large light stretch of the neck that is out of focus and this weakens the effect considerably, IMO.</td>', 'Color, line, lighting, and composition are super.  While I greatly appreciate the extreme softness of the background, I do wish the neck of the bird were not quite so out of focus.  While the bird''s eye is the natural focal point of the piece, man''s eye is naturally drawn to the large light stretch of the neck that is out of focus and this weakens the effect considerably, IMO.', '2005-07-20 12:37:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1550140, 204930, 33560, '<td valign="top">"Scratch me behind the ears.. I need a nap."   Perfect in every respect.</td>', '"Scratch me behind the ears.. I need a nap."   Perfect in every respect.', '2005-07-20 12:39:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1550152, 205433, 16053, '<td valign="top">It has got a strange look, almoust like diffuse glow. But it is very nice indeed. Nice pov.</td>', 'It has got a strange look, almoust like diffuse glow. But it is very nice indeed. Nice pov.', '2005-07-20 12:41:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1550156, 205383, 16053, '<td valign="top">Exelent use of b&amp;w and composition. 8</td>', 'Exelent use of b&w and composition. 8', '2005-07-20 12:42:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1550161, 204904, 33560, '<td valign="top">It''s a very difficult subject because of the white in well lit areas and the black in the shadows.  It looks like there are some blown highlights in the area below the eye and this detracts from the photo.  My own inclination is usually to crop this tightly, but I have seen a number of examples at this site in which a bird given more room somehow looks more natural, and I have the sense that this photo is a little crowded.</td>', 'It''s a very difficult subject because of the white in well lit areas and the black in the shadows.  It looks like there are some blown highlights in the area below the eye and this detracts from the photo.  My own inclination is usually to crop this tightly, but I have seen a number of examples at this site in which a bird given more room somehow looks more natural, and I have the sense that this photo is a little crowded.', '2005-07-20 12:43:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1550167, 205287, 16053, '<td valign="top">Goog tiger photo, but the all black backgroung gives it a fake feeling and look, and the way if blends (badly) with the grass doesen''t help.</td>', 'Goog tiger photo, but the all black backgroung gives it a fake feeling and look, and the way if blends (badly) with the grass doesen''t help.', '2005-07-20 12:45:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1550172, 204827, 16053, '<td valign="top">A bit overexposed for my taste but I can see why you did it this way, because you wanted all the eye detail. Very nice to see.</td>', 'A bit overexposed for my taste but I can see why you did it this way, because you wanted all the eye detail. Very nice to see.', '2005-07-20 12:46:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1550177, 203815, 33560, '<td valign="top">Patella''s Saggy Baggy IMAGE_ID=3726 looked much like this, compositionally.  He chose to enhance the textures using some unconventional unsharp mask settings and the effort won a ribbon.  Not sure the same trick would work twice, but I do think that it is in the textures that the strength of this photo lies, and I believe there are spots where sharpening would improve the textures.</td>', 'Patella''s Saggy Baggy IMAGE_ID=3726 looked much like this, compositionally.  He chose to enhance the textures using some unconventional unsharp mask settings and the effort won a ribbon.  Not sure the same trick would work twice, but I do think that it is in the textures that the strength of this photo lies, and I believe there are spots where sharpening would improve the textures.', '2005-07-20 12:48:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1550180, 205109, 16053, '<td valign="top">Awsome pic. I love all the detain in the horns. Here''s a photo that looks good to make a big poster in a living room.</td>', 'Awsome pic. I love all the detain in the horns. Here''s a photo that looks good to make a big poster in a living room.', '2005-07-20 12:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
