(1573950, 203753, 5082, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the nice comments... teh kangaroos are so red because, well, they are "reds".  Much more orange than the greys that were there.  I knew the tail on the kangaroo on the left was going to cost me, but I figured that cloning it out or masking it with a dodge would have been "cheating" a bit too much.</td>', 'Thanks for the nice comments... teh kangaroos are so red because, well, they are "reds".  Much more orange than the greys that were there.  I knew the tail on the kangaroo on the left was going to cost me, but I figured that cloning it out or masking it with a dodge would have been "cheating" a bit too much.', '2005-07-30 11:43:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1574157, 204771, 25553, '<td valign="top">I myself liked the blurred effect on the beak because I thought it showed the movement of the bird while catching the fish. At the same time I liked the sharp eye that lets you see the bird and connect with it. Thank you for your comments!</td>', 'I myself liked the blurred effect on the beak because I thought it showed the movement of the bird while catching the fish. At the same time I liked the sharp eye that lets you see the bird and connect with it. Thank you for your comments!', '2005-07-30 13:37:34.000000', NULL, 0),
